Translation patch: `SeqRepr::deserialize` for `Unknown`, `LeU32`, `LeU64`

Change: The loop `for _ in 0..len { seq.push(buf.parse(())?) }` (duplicated in both arms of `match T::SIZE`, and in the macro) moves into a helper `parse_items(len, buf, seq)` that takes the already-allocated `seq` by value, runs the loop and returns `Ok(Cow::Owned(seq))`; the arms call it on the local sub-buffer or on `buf`. `Vec::with_capacity(len)` stays where it was, before the `match`.
Why: Aeneas fails ("Could not match the contexts") on the loop when it runs over a local `ParseBuf` and the result is used after the `match`.
Behaviour: Identical: the allocation happens at the same point (so the same capacity-overflow panic / allocation failure for huge `len`), then the same parses run in the same order on the same buffer, with the same early `Err` returns; the helper is the extracted loop.

